  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GEO services Angola</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project partners, Fugro N.V. from the Netherlands and Augustos &amp; Augustos S.A. from Angola, propose to set up the first geo/technical laboratory in Angola to serve the building sector with a firm building base.They will start a joint venture company.At the moment, the expertise for every soil analysis, necessary for building and infrastructural works is flown in from all over the world, and soil samples are sent (mostly illegally) to laboratories all over the world for analysis. The partners want to start a laboratory in Luanda and train Angolan employees (postdoc level) to do surveys and analyse the soil samples taken.The project is risky as it will be difficult to find enough Angolan citizens with the necessary level and to keep them with the joint venture after the training has been completed. The partners believe that in the long run this project will become profitable.The impact is high, as this level of services is not yet available in Angola and the needs are high as the government is very actively building roads and bridges. Also, the private sector is booming in Angola which shows itself in a great number of buildings being erected in the major cities. A large number of training days will be spent to get the Angolan employees at the desired level.</narrative>
  </description>
